WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.490
Picture a mother who would protect
her only child with her life.

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.000
An early Buddhist text asks the
meditator to feel that kind of care,

3
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.000
without limit, for every living being.

4
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:15.180
Buddhists call this kind
of mind-training bhavana:

5
00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:18.110
cultivation, like tending a garden.

6
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.470
But when meditation makes
the mind calm and still,

7
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.240
is that calm a real
step towards awakening,

8
00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.600
or only a pleasant rest?

9
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.810
In this mission, you'll see where
meditation sits on the Eightfold Path,

10
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.840
and meet calm practice, called samatha.

11
00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.410
Then you'll try loving
kindness meditation,

12
00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.560
step by step, beginning with yourself.

13
00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:43.680
Your mission: weigh up whether
calm is a step towards awakening,

14
00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.480
or only a pleasant rest.
